Subject: [PATCH 0/3] iio: proximity: ST VL53L3CX on the Fairphone 5

The Fairphone 5 rear time-of-flight sensor is an ST VL53L3CX at I2C
address 0x29. Its model id is 0xEAAA. A VL53L1X reports 0xEACC. The
in-tree VL53L1X driver loads a 91-byte configuration from the VL53L1X
ultra lite driver and continues when the id does not match. That
configuration leaves the range register at zero on this part. The ST
VL53LX API, run in userspace, returns millimetres. This series does
not extend the VL53L1X driver and does not paste that API into the
kernel.

The binding patch adds compatible st,vl53l3cx to the existing
VL53L0X/VL53L1X schema and requires vdd-supply. The driver enables
vdd, releases XSHUT, and accepts only model id 0xEAAA. Distance
readout returns -EOPNOTSUPP until the VL53L3CX ranging sequence is
ported. The IIO channel is the ABI that sequence should fill: raw
millimetres, scale 0.001.

The board patch describes the sensor on GENI I2C9. The interrupt is
TLMM GPIO 48, edge falling. XSHUT is TLMM GPIO 49, active low. The
2.8 V rail is the existing fixed regulator VTOF_LDO_2P8, switched by
TLMM GPIO 141. It stays off until the driver enables vdd. It is not
marked regulator-boot-on.

Do not apply the devicetree patch on a kernel that still ranges
through i2c-dev. An OF I2C client at 0x29 reserves that address.

Base is sc7280-mainline v7.2.0-sc7280, commit f875148cc9fc ("fixup!
drivers: gpu: drm: panel: Initial FT8722 support").

Not mailed.

